From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0384-mem-audit-02-scratch-keep-switch.patch

Source: 0384-mem-audit-02-scratch-keep-switch.patch
Core patch, on core16 (through 0181). Paths are the submodule's. Use with mem-audit-04.

TickFrame keeps swizzle_data_buffer and unswizzle_data_buffer up to 64 MiB each between frames, so
up to 128 MiB stays held. Run62's largest uploads reached 64 and 288 MiB, so that ceiling is in
reach, but how much was really held is not logged. The swizzle one only grows when guest memory is
not contiguous, the unswizzle one only for converted images.

EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB=<0..64> in env.txt. Unset, or out of range, as before; try 8. At 8 at most
16 MiB stays held: up to 112 MiB back.

What it costs: a frame that needs more allocates it again, up to 2 x 64 MiB of churn a frame, and
when the pool is empty that can be refused where a kept buffer would not have been. That is why
this goes with mem-audit-04: without it a refused growth there ends the session.

TickFrame holds texture_cache.mutex and the buffers are only used within one call, so freeing them
more often adds no race.

Syntax-compiled for the PS5 target with warnings on, TextureCache instantiated for Vulkan and
OpenGL, through prepare-vulkan-port.py (same skipped anchors as before). Not built, not run on the
console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 1aceca5eb0..28f56411f5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -317,8 +317,26 @@ template <class P>
 void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
     // Upload buffers grown for one huge image (title 1's 341 MiB terrain layer pools) are freed
     // rather than kept for the rest of the session.
+    // EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB=<0..64>: keep less of each between frames. A frame that needs more
+    // allocates it again, which is what the two buffers exist to avoid, and that can be refused
+    // when the pool is empty (the image then keeps what it shows). Unset, as before.
+    static const size_t scratch_keep = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB");
+        if (value == nullptr) {
+            return LargeScratchCapacity;
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const unsigned long long mib = std::strtoull(value, &end, 10);
+        if (end == value || mib > (LargeScratchCapacity >> 20)) {
+            LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB={} is not 0 to {}: ignored", value,
+                        LargeScratchCapacity >> 20);
+            return LargeScratchCapacity;
+        }
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Upload scratch buffers keep at most {} MiB each", mib);
+        return static_cast<size_t>(mib) << 20;
+    }();
     for (auto* const scratch : {&swizzle_data_buffer, &unswizzle_data_buffer}) {
-        if (scratch->capacity() > LargeScratchCapacity) {
+        if (scratch->capacity() > scratch_keep) {
             scratch->release();
         }
     }
